The Cailleach? Aye, I know her well enough, though I keep my distance when the mist rolls in off the bog. She’s a wise woman, sure, but there’s a certain... stillness about her that makes the hair on yer arms stand up. Ye’d best mind yer step if ye’re goin’ near the sí, for the Fair Folk don’t take kindly to strangers wanderin’ in their domain.
