Ah, I remember it well, though I wish I didn't, for the boy's cry still rings in my ears. 'Twas a nasty break, right through the tibia, and I spent three nights splinting it with ash wood while his mother wept in the corner. We got it set true in the end, though he did walk with a limp for a good year or two.
